Trina AX

This repository contains the filtered Team AX core, the shared cloud
protocols, and the Trina edition branding. The separately licensed hosting
control plane (ee/), the Trina paid operations code and the trina.app website
are not part of this repository or its history; they stay in the private
trina-ax-core repository. See docs/UPSTREAM.md for provenance and docs/PUBLICATION.md for
publication conditions.

Preserve the copyright notices and authorship of Team AX and incorporated
third-party components. The accompanying LICENSE preserves the Team AX
GNU Affero General Public License version 3 text. Trina edition additions
are designated AGPL-3.0-only; this does not grant rights to third-party or
separately licensed material.

Component-specific scope:
- shared/src/cloud-protocol/ has its own MIT LICENSE, which is retained.
- ee/ (the hosting control plane) is excluded and stays private. The Trina
  edition loads its contracts at run time from a separate checkout
  (TRINA_CORE_ROOT); no ee/ code or grant is included here.
- Saram/chat-proto-derived code: the copyright holder (Potenlab) confirmed
  on 2026-10-27 that it may be published under AGPL-3.0-only.
- PowerPoint previews use @aiden0z/pptx-renderer@1.4.0 (Apache-2.0). Its
  bundle includes mtx-decompressor (MPL-2.0, unmodified) and a mechanical
  subset of ECMA-376 preset-shape definitions under the Ecma copyright notice.
  The package ships these notices in its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and licenses/;
  web builds copy its LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md to web/dist/licenses/.
  It replaces pptx-preview@1.0.7, whose author restricts source publication.
- The historical website license (Apache-2.0) and Trina Inc. attribution
  stay in editions/trina/branding/. The website source, its fonts and their
  notices moved to trina-ax-core with the website.

